X:38
T:Polka. WmT.038
B:Wm Titley MS, Shropshire UK, circa1860s
N:The number of beats in most bars are at odds to the 2/4 time signature and too problematical to attempt to 'correct',
N:so I've transcribed the tune as is in the ms.
N:The first time bar in the C part is written as a dotted crotchet with a single bar across the stem,
N:which is a short cut for three quavers. There isn't an ABC way of writing this as far as I am aware,
N:so I have written it out as the three crotchets.
