X:78
T:Musards 43 set No. 3. WmT.078
B:Wm Titley MS, Shropshire UK, circa1860s
N:The key signature is writen as if it was in the key of A in the treble clef although the clef is the bass clef.
N:I've assumed the key of A is meant
N:And then on the third line the key signature is again writen as if it was in the key of F in the treble clef although the clef is the bass clef.
N:I've assumed the key of F is meant
N:Bars 2 is written with a measure repeat sing (due volte). I'm not aware of an abc notation for this
N:so I've written the bars out in full.
N:Bar 4 (after the initial 2 bars rest) is written with a slur and the word trio under it,
N:which I have interpreted as a triplet with not s lot of confidence.
N:There is a one quaver rest anacrucis in bar 1 of the second line in the ms
N:Bar 7 of the second line has a minim in the ms - I have written this as a dotted minim to give the right number of beats in thst bar
N:There is a two quaver rest anacrucis in bar 1 of the third line in the ms
