X:220
T:Uncle Tom's Cabin Quadrille 2. WmT.220
B:Wm Titley MS, Shropshire UK, circa1860s
N:Bar 1 of the B music is written as a minim with a diagonal bar across the stem in the ms.
N:This means divide the note into quavers. I don't think there is
N:an ABC notation for this so I have written these bars out as four quavers.
M:2/4
L:1/8
